Most warlocks in classic WoW are seen with voidwalkers because voidwalkers provide useful tanking and threat generation abilities (Torment and Suffering) that help manage mobs and reduce the risk of pulling additional enemies. This is particularly beneficial for leveling and questing, where managing multiple mobs is common. Additionally, the voidwalker's Sacrifice ability can shield the warlock, providing a safety net in dangerous situations. [end of text]


